<title>GERMANY: Siemens says still in sick pay talks.</title>
<headline>Siemens says still in sick pay talks.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering giant Siemens AG said on Tuesday it was still in talks with trade unions on whether to implement a 20 percent cut in sick pay.</p>
<p>A spokesman in Munich declined to confirm a statement by the IG Metall union that Siemens had agreed to continue paying full sick pay.</p>
<p>Siemens last week announced that it would join companies opting to implement sick pay cuts under rules which have now taken effect. That decision outraged trade unions, which said 100 percent sick pay was written into their work contracts.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
